# SABOTAGE: the P17 own-org analytics page (and the read beneath it) DISCARDS the reason it cannot
# answer. A session with no resolved org, a role the gate REFUSES, an unmounted seam, and a rollup
# read that RAISED all render as "No activation data yet." — a statement about the org's data that
# the request never observed (ADR-014/024/026). On the one surface a tenant reads insights on, that
# is exactly the confusion the fix exists to remove: an operator cannot tell a host that has emitted
# no events from an unmigrated table or a role that was withheld from them.
#
# Aimed at the SILENCE contract ONLY (`AnalyticsReads.read/3`'s reason + `AnalyticsLive`'s use of it):
# the org-scoped read, the shipped k-anonymity floor, the real membership role and the `?org=`-forge
# refusal are all untouched, so the page still reads the RIGHT org on the RIGHT floor — it simply
# cannot say that it failed. Two collapses, one defect: the read stops naming its reason (and reports
# a failed read as an answered empty one), and the page loses every per-silence statement it had,
# including the NEXT STEP that cleared it (a refused role -> the team settings that grant it; an
# unwired seam -> the mount docs; a failed read -> the runbook). The page keeps the shared shell — it
# is the SILENCE that disappears into the empty state, which is what made those states actionable
# rather than merely legible.
#
# The next-step RESOLUTION (`unread_next_step/3` and its helpers) is deliberately LEFT IN PLACE: the
# defect is that the page never renders a reason at all, and the mapping is a public function the
# suite calls directly, so removing it would turn this sabotage into a missing-function COMPILE error
# instead of a page that lies. `unread_title/1`/`unread_body/1` go because nothing references them
# once the branch is gone, and the `unread_state/1` import goes with the branch that used it.
#
# TWO ANALYSIS WARNINGS ARE EXPECTED, and they are part of what makes this patch a page that lies
# rather than a broken build: with the reason discarded, `read/3`'s second branch is unreachable
# (`dynamic(nil)`) and `org_id/1`'s nil clause can no longer be reached from `silence/2`. The replay
# runs `mix test` in the patch's APP (never the ship gate's `--warnings-as-errors` compile), so
# neither is confined or silenced — they are reported here rather than papered over.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/tenant_analytics_test.exs test/samen/web/tenant_analytics_route_e2e_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: read/3 names the silence
# MUST_FAIL: a rollup that cannot be read is :read_failed
# MUST_FAIL: the HONEST no-org state
# MUST_FAIL: a session with no mount
# MUST_FAIL: every silence is a DISTINCT state
# MUST_FAIL: a state with no honest next step renders no affordance at all
# MUST_FAIL: the refusal state names the role and renders no cell at all
# MUST_FAIL: one plain-language sentence per silence
# MUST_FAIL: every state renders INSIDE the main panel of the shared shell
# MUST_FAIL: a REAL :viewer member is refused with :not_authorized
# MUST_FAIL: an authenticated principal with NO resolved org says so
# MUST_FAIL: a refused role is handed the ONE step that clears it
# MUST_FAIL: a host that declares no settings path still STATES the step
# MUST_FAIL: the wiring gap and the failed read name their doc
# MUST_FAIL: the load/2 WIRING carries the step
